From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Mar 2026 11:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net: expose forward-path helpers for bridge flow offload

Airoha bridge and WLAN PPE offload paths need to reuse the bridge FDB
lookup from outside bridge core code so that their own forward-path
resolution sees the same entries.

The forward path walk itself comes from dev_fill_forward_path(), which
takes a net_device_path_ctx from the caller, so only the FDB lookup still
has to be exported.

Based on MediaTek SDK bridge flow offload work.

Co-authored-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 net/bridge/br_fdb.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -266,6 +266,7 @@ struct net_bridge_fdb_entry *br_fdb_find_rcu(struct net_bridge *br,
 {
 	return fdb_find_rcu(&br->fdb_hash_tbl, addr, vid);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(br_fdb_find_rcu);
 
 /* When a static FDB entry is added, the mac address from the entry is
  * added to the bridge private HW address list and all required ports
